  "worked_solution": "- Statement I is false. The function has an infinite discontinuity at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-5$ it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is continuous at $x=0$ and doesn't have a corner point, a  cusp, or a vertical tangent.\n\nTherefore, only statement III  is true.",
